+### [Score-based Densification](4705-score-based-densification.md)
+A constructive densification strategy that controls model size by adding new Gaussians only to those primitives that maximize a specific quality score, adhering to a pre-defined user budget. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting which relies on aggressive pruning and splitting without strict size caps, this method ensures the final model size is predictable and bounded, avoiding the optimization instability caused by large-scale culling. It is designed for scenarios where hardware memory or storage constraints require a fixed-capacity output.
 
-### GroupFlow [6351-groupflow.md]
-GroupFlow is a motion compression technique for dynamic 3D Gaussian Splatting that distills per-Gaussian neural deformation fields into shared SE(3) transformations for groupwise motion [S1]. It solves the computational bottleneck of evaluating individual neural networks for every Gaussian primitive at every timestep, reducing rendering and training costs by replacing $N$ per-Gaussian transformations with $J$ per-group transformations [S1]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Gaussian Densification](4314-gaussian-densification.md) by focusing on temporal motion efficiency rather than spatial density management, though it often operates in conjunction with densification strategies to maintain scene fidelity.
+### [GroupFlow](6351-groupflow.md)
+GroupFlow is a motion compression technique for dynamic 3D Gaussian Splatting that replaces per-Gaussian neural deformation fields with shared SE(3) transformations for groups of Gaussians. It solves the computational bottleneck of evaluating individual deformation networks for every Gaussian at every timestep, accelerating rendering by up to 13.71× and reducing training time by 2.53× while maintaining high image quality. Unlike methods that retain per-Gaussian parameters, GroupFlow distills dense motion into a smaller set of groupwise rigid-body trajectories, regularizing noisy motion estimates.
 
